<p>I tried to cut it down, but all the info given would be important in-universe for people reading it to know. I can't just [DATA EXPUNGED FOR BEING BORING TO READ]. Well, I could, but I don't think it'd be a good idea. Yes, heavily abridging the info about the nature and behaviour of -2 would get you to the out-of-universe payoff faster because it's not actually all that important to the story, but in-universe the part that wants to gnaw your feet off is the most important thing to know about in detail.</p>
<p>(e: Also, articles that lack answers/implication of answers to obvious, easily-testable questions bug me. They've been containing this one for literally decades, so I expect there to be oodles and gobs of data on the things that can be tested or examined relatively easily. I've relegated the vast majority of it to the realm of not-included supplemental files, but what I've got sans the addenda is the minimum of what I would expect of the in-universe main file.)</p>

